.TH MACOSX-CROSS-LDD 1 "September 2026" "macosx-cross @MACOSX_CROSS_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
macosx-cross-ldd \- inspect Mach-O dynamic library dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macosx-cross-ldd
.RB [ \-\-macosx-sdk =VERSION ]
.RB [ \-\-target =TARGET ]
.RB [ \-\-arch =ARCH ]
.RB [ \-\-recursive ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.I mach-o-file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macosx-cross-ldd
inspects the dynamic library dependencies of a Mach-O executable or library
using
.B llvm-otool .

Dependencies are read from the Mach-O load commands using
.B "llvm-otool -L"
and resolved against the selected macOS SDK, framework directories,
metadata-defined library search paths, and Mach-O runtime path mechanisms.

The program supports
.B @loader_path ,
.B @executable_path ,
and
.B @rpath
dependency references.

Framework dependencies are resolved against the framework directories
provided by the selected SDK.

By default, only the direct dependencies of the input file are displayed.
Use
.B --recursive
to recursively inspect the dependencies of resolved libraries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-macosx-sdk =VERSION
Select the macOS SDK version to use.

The SDK must exist below the macosx-cross SDK directory.

For example:

.RS
.nf
--macosx-sdk=10.9
--macosx-sdk=14.5
--macosx-sdk=15.5
.fi
.RE

If omitted, the default SDK root is used.

.TP
.BR \-\-target =TARGET
Select the target triple.

Supported target families include:

.RS
.nf
x86_64-apple-darwin
arm64-apple-darwin
arm64e-apple-darwin

x86_64-apple-ios
arm64-apple-ios

arm64-apple-ios-macabi
.fi
.RE

The target is required.

The target is also used to select architecture defaults and the appropriate
SDK metadata search paths.

.TP
.BR \-\-arch =ARCH
Select the Mach-O architecture passed to
.B llvm-otool .

Supported examples include:

.RS
.nf
x86_64
arm64
arm64e
.fi
.RE

If omitted, the architecture is inferred from the target.

.TP
.B \-\-recursive
Recursively resolve dependencies.

Without this option, only the dependencies directly referenced by the input
file are displayed.

.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing and treat the following argument as the input file.
.SH OUTPUT
The input file is printed first, followed by each dependency and its
resolved path.

A successfully resolved dependency is displayed as:

.RS
.nf
        DEPENDENCY => /resolved/path
.fi
.RE

When a dependency cannot be resolved:

.RS
.nf
        DEPENDENCY => not found
.fi
.RE

Recursive dependencies are indented with an additional tab for each level.
.SH DEPENDENCY RESOLUTION
Dependencies are resolved using the following mechanisms.

.TP
.B @loader_path
The directory containing the Mach-O file currently being inspected is used
as
.B @loader_path .

.TP
.B @executable_path
The directory containing the original executable is used as
.B @executable_path .

.TP
.B @rpath
RPATH entries from the Mach-O loader are expanded and searched.

RPATH entries from the original executable are also considered when
inspecting a dependency.

.TP
.B Frameworks
Framework dependencies are resolved against framework directories in the
selected SDK, including:

.RS
.nf
System/Library/Frameworks
Library/Frameworks
System/Library/PrivateFrameworks
Library/PrivateFrameworks
.fi
.RE

Versioned framework layouts using
.B Versions/Current
and
.B Versions/A
are supported.

.TP
.B Absolute paths
Absolute dependency paths are first interpreted relative to the selected
SDK.

For example:

.RS
.nf
/usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib
.fi
.RE

is searched as:

.RS
.nf
<SDK>/usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Search paths
Metadata-defined library search paths are used in addition to the standard
SDK library and framework directories.

For iOS targets,
.B LIBRARY_IOS_SEARCH_PATHS
is used.

For macOS targets,
.B LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS
is used.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLVM_OTOOL
Path to the
.B llvm-otool
executable.

If unset, the program searches for:

.RS
.nf
llvm-otool-19
llvm-otool
/usr/bin/llvm-otool-19
/usr/bin/llvm-otool
/bin/llvm-otool-19
/bin/llvm-otool
.fi
.RE

The first executable found is used.

.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_VERSION
Default SDK version when
.B --macosx-sdk
is not specified.

.TP
.B MACOSX_TARGET
Default target triple when
.B --target
is not specified.

.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_ARCHS
Architecture list for macOS SDK targets.

.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_IOS_ARCHS
Architecture list for iOS targets.

.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_IOSMAC_ARCHS
Architecture list for iOS Mac Catalyst targets.

.TP
.B LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional library search paths for macOS targets.

.TP
.B LIBRARY_IOS_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional library search paths for iOS targets.

.TP
.B IOS_UNZIPPERED_TWIN_PREFIX_PATH
Optional prefix used when resolving absolute dependencies and additional
iOS SDK library and framework paths.
.SH SDK METADATA
When an SDK is selected,
.B macosx-cross-ldd
loads:

.RS
.nf
<SDK>/.metadata
.fi
.RE

The metadata can provide architecture lists and additional library search
paths used during dependency resolution.
.SH MACH-O SUPPORT
The input file must be a Mach-O file.

The following Mach-O magic values are recognized:

.RS
.nf
feedface
cefaedfe
feedfacf
cffaedfe
cafebabe
bebafeca
cafebabf
bfbafeca
.fi
.RE

Both regular Mach-O files and universal/fat Mach-O files are recognized.

The selected architecture is passed to
.B llvm-otool
when
.B --arch
is specified or inferred.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@
macosx-cross installation root.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk
Installed SDK directory.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION
Individual macOS SDK.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION/.metadata
SDK metadata used for dependency resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect an x86_64 macOS executable:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-ldd \\
    --macosx-sdk=10.9 \\
    --target=x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    ./test
.fi
.RE

Inspect an arm64 macOS executable recursively:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-ldd \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    --recursive \\
    ./test
.fi
.RE

Explicitly select an architecture:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-ldd \\
    --macosx-sdk=15.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    --arch=arm64 \\
    ./test
.fi
.RE

Inspect an iOS binary:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-ldd \\
    --macosx-sdk=18.0 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-ios \\
    ./test
.fi
.RE

Use a custom llvm-otool:

.RS
.nf
LLVM_OTOOL=/opt/llvm/bin/llvm-otool \\
macosx-cross-ldd \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    ./test
.fi
.RE

Use environment variables instead of command-line options:

.RS
.nf
MACOSX_SDK_VERSION=14.5 \\
MACOSX_TARGET=arm64-apple-darwin \\
macosx-cross-ldd ./test
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The input Mach-O file was successfully inspected.

Individual dependencies may still be reported as
.B "not found"
while the command exits successfully.

.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, including an invalid input file, missing SDK, missing
target, unsupported architecture, unknown option, or unavailable
.B llvm-otool .
.SH NOTES
.B macosx-cross-ldd
is intended for inspecting cross-compiled Apple binaries on non-macOS
hosts.

It does not execute the Mach-O binary and does not use the host system's
dynamic linker.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR macosx-cross (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang++ (1),
.BR llvm-otool (1)
